// src/data/EXT_MATH/EM_07A/diagrams.js
// Teaching diagrams for EM_07A — Bounds, Inequalities & Simultaneous
// Equations. Every coordinate was computed and every <text> written out
// literally; edit by hand freely.
//
// House rules (docs/svg-diagrams.md, docs/ext-math-course.md §6):
//  · every diagram opens with a white plate, so it reads on a light OR dark slide;
//  · every <text> is literal, because `npm run audit:svg` reads only literal text;
//  · angles, bearings and graphs are drawn to scale from the question's numbers,
//    so a student can check an answer against the picture;
//  · a hotspot's figure marks the labels it needs `class="keep"` — the hotspot
//    strips every other label, so the answer letters vanish and the rest stay.
//  · a region is shaded the way the IGCSE paper shades it: grey where the
//    inequalities fail, the region R left white.
//
//   BOUNDS_LINE       12.6 m to 1 d.p.: the band 12.55 ≤ l < 12.65
//   TIME_ZONES        Paris → London timetable, and counting on in one time zone
//   FLIP              × (−1) swaps the order: −3 < 2 but 3 > −2
//   SOLVE_LINE        x > −3 on a number line
//   CIRCLES           open for < and >, filled for ≤ and ≥
//   REGION_KEY        x > 1, y ≥ 1, x + y ≤ 7 — dashed and solid lines, R white
//   REGION_PICK       the same region with four test points (hotspot)
//   GRADIENT          A(−1, 1), C(2, 7): rise 6, run 3
//   AREA_TRI          legs x and 2x + 1, area 18
//   SIM_LINES         x + y = 10 and x − y = 4 cross at (7, 3)
//   ELIM_COLUMNS      elimination in columns: the y column cancels
//   SUB_ARROW         substitution: y = 2x − 1 goes into the other equation
//   WB_TIMETABLE      Hanoi → Singapore, local times (Practice)
//   WB_PARALLELOGRAM  angles in x and y (Book Problems)
//   WB_AREA_TRI       legs x and 2x − 1, area 14 (Book Problems)

